@@ -0,0 +1,11 @@
+Feature: Deleting todos
+  As a user
+  I want to remove a todo I no longer need
+  So that my list stays relevant
+
+  Scenario: Deleting a todo via its destroy button
+    Given the app is loaded with a todo "Buy groceries" and a todo "Walk the dog"
+    When the user clicks the destroy button on the todo "Buy groceries"
+    Then the todo "Buy groceries" is not displayed
+    And the todo "Walk the dog" is displayed in the list
+    And the todo counter displays "1 item left"
diff --git a/features/editing-todos.feature b/features/editing-todos.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..53baf53
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/editing-todos.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,37 @@
+Feature: Editing todos
+  As a user
+  I want to edit existing todos
+  So that I can correct or update their titles
+
+  Scenario: Activating edit mode with double-click
+    Given the app is loaded with a todo "Buy groceries"
+    When the user double-clicks the todo "Buy groceries"
+    Then the todo "Buy groceries" is in editing mode
+    And the edit input contains "Buy groceries"
+    And the edit input is focused
+
+  Scenario: Saving an edit on Enter
+    Given the app is loaded with a todo "Buy groceries"
+    When the user double-clicks the todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the user types "Buy organic groceries" in the edit input and presses Enter
+    Then a todo "Buy organic groceries" is displayed in the list
+    And the todo "Buy organic groceries" is not in editing mode
+
+  Scenario: Saving an edit on blur
+    Given the app is loaded with a todo "Buy groceries"
+    When the user double-clicks the todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the user types "Buy organic groceries" in the edit input and blurs
+    Then a todo "Buy organic groceries" is displayed in the list
+
+  Scenario: Deleting a todo by clearing its edit input
+    Given the app is loaded with a todo "Buy groceries"
+    When the user double-clicks the todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the user clears the edit input and presses Enter
+    Then no todos are displayed
+
+  Scenario: Discarding an edit on Escape
+    Given the app is loaded with a todo "Buy groceries"
+    When the user double-clicks the todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the user types "Something else" in the edit input and presses Escape
+    Then a todo "Buy groceries" is displayed in the list
+    And the todo "Buy groceries" is not in editing mode
diff --git a/features/mark-all-complete.feature b/features/mark-all-complete.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..27682cc
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/mark-all-complete.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,28 @@
+Feature: Mark all as complete
+  As a user
+  I want to mark all todos as complete at once
+  So that I can quickly complete my entire list
+
+  Scenario: Marking all todos as complete
+    Given the app is loaded with an incomplete todo "Task A" and an incomplete todo "Task B"
+    When the user clicks the Mark all as complete checkbox
+    Then the todo "Task A" is marked as completed
+    And the todo "Task B" is marked as completed
+    And the Mark all as complete checkbox is checked
+    And the todo counter displays "0 items left"
+
+  Scenario: Unmarking all todos when all are complete
+    Given the app is loaded with a completed todo "Task A" and a completed todo "Task B"
+    Then the Mark all as complete checkbox is checked
+    When the user clicks the Mark all as complete checkbox
+    Then the todo "Task A" is not marked as completed
+    And the todo "Task B" is not marked as completed
+    And the Mark all as complete checkbox is not checked
+
+  Scenario: Mark all checkbox syncs with individual toggle states
+    Given the app is loaded with an incomplete todo "Task A" and a completed todo "Task B"
+    Then the Mark all as complete checkbox is not checked
+    When the user clicks the toggle checkbox on the todo "Task A"
+    Then the Mark all as complete checkbox is checked
+    When the user clicks the toggle checkbox on the todo "Task A"
+    Then the Mark all as complete checkbox is not checked
diff --git a/features/new-todo-creation.feature b/features/new-todo-creation.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..e1eeef5
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/new-todo-creation.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,33 @@
+Feature: New todo creation
+  As a user
+  I want to add todos to my list
+  So that I can track tasks I need to complete
+
+  Scenario: Creating a todo with Enter key
+    Given the app is loaded with no todos
+    When the user types "Buy groceries" in the new todo input and presses Enter
+    Then a todo "Buy groceries" is displayed in the list
+    And the new todo input is empty
+    And the todo counter displays "1 item left"
+
+  Scenario: Trimming whitespace from new todo titles
+    Given the app is loaded with no todos
+    When the user types "  Buy groceries  " in the new todo input and presses Enter
+    Then a todo "Buy groceries" is displayed in the list
+    And the new todo input is empty
+
+  Scenario: Not creating a todo from empty or whitespace-only input
+    Given the app is loaded with no todos
+    When the user types "   " in the new todo input and presses Enter
+    Then no todos are displayed
+    And the new todo input is empty
+
+  Scenario: New todo input is focused on page load
+    Given the app is loaded with no todos
+    Then the new todo input is focused
+
+  Scenario: Adding a second todo
+    Given the app is loaded with a todo "First task"
+    When the user types "Second task" in the new todo input and presses Enter
+    Then two todos are displayed
+    And the todo counter displays "2 items left"
diff --git a/features/persistence.feature b/features/persistence.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..743597c
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/persistence.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,29 @@
+Feature: Persistence
+  As a user
+  I want my todos to survive page reloads
+  So that I do not lose my data
+
+  Scenario: Todos persist across page reload
+    Given the app is loaded with a todo "Buy groceries" and a todo "Walk the dog"
+    And the user clicks the toggle checkbox on the todo "Buy groceries"
+    When the page is reloaded
+    Then a todo "Buy groceries" is displayed in the list
+    And the todo "Buy groceries" is marked as completed
+    And the todo "Walk the dog" is displayed in the list
+    And the todo "Walk the dog" is not marked as completed
+    And the todo counter displays "1 item left"
+
+  Scenario: Deleted todos do not reappear on reload
+    Given the app is loaded with a todo "Buy groceries" and a todo "Walk the dog"
+    When the user clicks the destroy button on the todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the page is reloaded
+    Then the todo "Buy groceries" is not displayed
+    And the todo "Walk the dog" is displayed in the list
+
+  Scenario: Edited todos persist their new title across reload
+    Given the app is loaded with a todo "Buy groceries"
+    When the user double-clicks the todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the user types "Buy organic groceries" in the edit input and presses Enter
+    And the page is reloaded
+    Then a todo "Buy organic groceries" is displayed in the list
+    And the todo "Buy groceries" is not displayed
diff --git a/features/routing.feature b/features/routing.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..840fb74
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/routing.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,37 @@
+Feature: Routing and filtering
+  As a user
+  I want to filter todos by their completion status
+  So that I can focus on active or completed items
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded with an incomplete todo "Active task" and a completed todo "Done task"
+
+  Scenario: All route shows every todo
+    When the user navigates to "#/"
+    Then the todo "Active task" is displayed in the list
+    And the todo "Done task" is displayed in the list
+    And the "All" filter link is selected
+
+  Scenario: Active route shows only incomplete todos
+    When the user navigates to "#/active"
+    Then the todo "Active task" is displayed in the list
+    And the todo "Done task" is not displayed
+    And the "Active" filter link is selected
+
+  Scenario: Completed route shows only completed todos
+    When the user navigates to "#/completed"
+    Then the todo "Active task" is not displayed
+    And the todo "Done task" is displayed in the list
+    And the "Completed" filter link is selected
+
+  Scenario: Completing a todo hides it from the active filter
+    When the user navigates to "#/active"
+    Then the todo "Active task" is displayed in the list
+    When the user clicks the toggle checkbox on the todo "Active task"
+    Then the todo "Active task" is not displayed
+
+  Scenario: All filter is the default route
+    When the app is loaded fresh
+    Then the "All" filter link is selected
+    And the todo "Active task" is displayed in the list
+    And the todo "Done task" is displayed in the list
